AI Video Studio
Parts of this project are adapted from other open source work. Each entry says what was taken and what was changed.

video-shotcraft (https://github.com/Vincentwei1021/video-shotcraft)
Copyright the video-shotcraft authors. Licensed under the Apache License, Version 2.0
(a copy is in third_party/video-shotcraft/LICENSE).

Adapted from it, rewritten for this project's blocks, pipeline and Vietnamese-language workflow:
  - remotion/camera/noise.ts: the deterministic PRNG (mulberry32) and hand-held drift (handheld), from assets/lib/helpers.
  - remotion/camera/moves.ts, remotion/camera/DepthStage.tsx: the idea of a perspective ("2.5D") camera over a still
    picture and of multiplane layers moving at different speeds (far, middle, near), from assets/lib/PageCam.tsx and
    the depth-layer-moves shot recipe. The moves, poses and layers here are new code.
  - src/core/audio/sfx.ts and the SFX cue hooks of the blocks: the sound-design restraint rules (short sounds, quiet
    under the voice, spacing between cues, one big hit at a time) from references/sound-design.md and
    references/aesthetic-rules.md.
  - src/core/quality/checks (variety, spoken, av-health), design legibility floors in src/core/domain/design.ts and
    the story/pace guidance in src/core/tasks/story.ts: derived from the review rules in references/aesthetic-rules.md,
    references/final-review.md and the "inspect the rendered frames" practice of references/pipeline.md.
  - remotion/shots/text/*: the 27 text shots (entrances and cycling lines) are new implementations of the typography
    recipes of video-shotcraft (blur-slide, brace-expand, countdown-arc-scatter, flying-words, glitch-cycle,
    gradient-word-sweep, lead-word-zoom-assemble, marker-underline-title, outline-word-fill, paper-title-card, pill-slot-cycle,
    text-column-converge, title-demote-to-label, type-assembly-moves, type-entrance-moves, type-rhythm-sync,
    typewriter-moves, vertical-word-roll-blur-cycle, word-relay-filmstrip, word-relay-geometry). The motion ideas are theirs;
    the code, content slots and timings are ours.
  - remotion/shots/transitions.tsx: the 17 scene entrances are new implementations of the transition recipes (bottom-push-stack-wipe,
    page-turn barn-door-split, blinds-slice, glitch-displace, ink-bleed-reveal, hidden-cut light leak, card-flip-reveal,
    mosaic-reframe, circle-match-iris, and the shot-transition wipes) of video-shotcraft, adapted to start the incoming scene.
  - remotion/camera/moves.ts (bullet-time, pull-back, drone-dive, graze-slide, steep-slide, handheld-push) and remotion/shots/fx.tsx
    (nine light overlays): new implementations of the tension / space / overhead / steep-tilt camera recipes and of the light-play,
    spotlight-sweep, scan-bracket, fui-hud, glow-flyline and impact-feedback effect recipes.
  - remotion/camera/cuts.tsx (rhythm cuts) and remotion/blocks/{timeline,gauge,dots}.tsx: new implementations of the rhythm recipes
    (beat-cut-moves, panel-grid-moves, rhythm-interrupt-moves, quad-split-parallel-scenes, sakuga-timing-shift) and of the data
    recipes (timeline-travel, gauge-readout-moves, chart-live-moves unit-dot-swarm).
  - Intro/outro vocabulary (design.ts anims materialize, stamp, glitch, crash-in, drop; shapes glow, rays, grid; the marquee layer): new
    implementations of the opening and outro recipes (letterspace-materialize, brand-ink-open, grain-dissolve, neon-triple-marquee,
    magician-card-flourish, logo-shrink-wordmark-lockup).

No audio, image or other media files from video-shotcraft are included. Sound effects are synthesised on the user's
machine with ffmpeg (src/server/adapters/sfx/sfx.service.ts), and a person may add their own files.
